    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Description\n\nThe table passed to `set_picker_query` will be updated afterward, which I think is not the intended behavior?\n\n```lua\nq = {\"abc\"}\n\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({\n\tmappings = {\n\t\tw = {\n\t\t\tchar = \"<c-w>\",\n\t\t\tfunc = function()\n\t\t\t\trequire(\"mini.pick\").set_picker_query(q)\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t},\n\t\te = {\n\t\t\tchar = \"<c-e>\",\n\t\t\tfunc = function()\n\t\t\t\tvim.print(q)\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t},\n\t},\n})\n```\n\n1. `:Pick help`\n2. press `<c-w>`\n3. press `x`\n4. press `<c-e>`\n\nexpect: `{\"abc\"}`\nactual: `{\"abc\", \"x\"}`",
